winewayland: scope the owned-subsurface rule to CAPTION-LESS windows

A wl_subsurface is positioned by US -- that is the entire point of the previous
commit, and what makes cross-window coordinates exact again. But it also means
the COMPOSITOR cannot move it. So anything the user drags by a title bar must
stay an xdg_toplevel, and a caption is exactly that signal.

The first cut converted EVERY managed owned window, which would have taken
Photoshop's Image Size, Preferences, Export Settings and every other owned
dialog with it -- windows people move constantly. That was casting far wider
than the defect needed.

The discriminator came from the user, describing the panel the fix was written
for: "This panel can't move and was never designed to move." A caption-less
owned tool window has nothing to lose by becoming a subsurface; a captioned
dialog has everything to lose. Captioned owned windows stay the business of
NEUTRON_DOCK_OWNED, which is opt-in for precisely that reason.

Also folds in the user's verification of the previous commit: hide/reshow of the
Button Editor works correctly, so the empty-subsurface trap from the Lightroom
filmstrip work does not bite here.

--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
@@ -780,11 +780,21 @@
         if (neutron_owned_subsurface() && managed && !owner && toplevel == hwnd)
         {
             HWND gwowner = NtUserGetWindowRelative( hwnd, GW_OWNER );
+            DWORD st = NtUserGetWindowLongW( hwnd, GWL_STYLE );
 
             /* GW_OWNER is NULL for exactly the windows this is meant to catch; owner_hint is the
              * value win32u actually passed us and it is correct. */
             if (!gwowner) gwowner = owner_hint;
-            if (gwowner && gwowner != hwnd && NtUserIsWindowVisible( gwowner ))
+
+            /* ⛔ CAPTION-LESS ONLY. A subsurface is positioned by us, which is the whole point --
+             * but it also means the COMPOSITOR cannot move it, so anything the user drags by a
+             * title bar must stay an xdg_toplevel. A caption is exactly that signal. The user, on
+             * the panel this was written for: "This panel can't move and was never designed to
+             * move" -- so it loses nothing, while Image Size / Preferences / Export Settings keep
+             * the behaviour people expect. Captioned owned windows remain the business of
+             * NEUTRON_DOCK_OWNED above, which is opt-in for that reason. */
+            if (gwowner && gwowner != hwnd && !(st & WS_CAPTION) &&
+                NtUserIsWindowVisible( gwowner ))
             {
                 ERR( "neutron-ownedsub: hwnd=%p (style=%08x ex=%08x) -> SUBSURFACE of owner=%p "
                      "so its position is ours to set, not the compositor's\n",
